        "geology": "The geology of Island consists of 3% metamorphosed sedimentary and volcanic rocks; 31% ophiolites; 8% Tertiary sedimentary and volcanic rocks; 26% granites and 32% marine sediments & Quaternary deposits.",
        "hydrology": "The island is rich in both springs and streams. The SNO monitoring network includes  23 Streams basins, 21 cold springs and 2 hot springs. The springs of these streams originate from the Saos Mountain (with highest altitude 1.661m). The climate of the island is of a Mediterranean type, and characterized by rainy and snowy winters, and hot and dry summers. The mean annual rainfall is 605 mm. The island presents very steep slopes, ranging between 15o and 30o.",
        "soils": null,
        "vegetation": "The main land uses are forests (42.8%), agricultural land (25.2%) and pasture (24.4%)."
